# Silverbough Estate -- walled manor grounds (26x22 blocks = 52x44 steps)
#
# Pitch: a lord's estate at the end of a quiet lane. You come in through a white-fenced
# gate where a gatekeeper stands in the gap (he can step aside after a story flag). A
# straight hedged avenue runs north to a fountain forecourt and a long, two-storey
# traditional manor. To the west is a formal hedge maze built from single-step hedges
# (small-tree blocks 3c/5c/5d/60, so walls are one step thick), with an item ball at its
# deepest dead end and three hidden items in the others. To the east is an ornamental
# pond crossed by a plank boardwalk (89) to a little tea pavilion on its own lawn. The NW
# lawn is an apricorn orchard. A servants' cottage beside the manor has its own door.
#
# Manor: 9 blocks (18 steps) wide, 3 block rows tall = roof + 2 storeys.
#   2c 2a*7 2d / 22 2b*7 23 / 26 2b 2b 2b 27 2b 2b 2b 2f
#   FRONT DOOR = step (24, 9) (block 12,4; 27's door is its bottom-left quadrant).
#   Player steps out to (24,10). Centre of facade is between steps 24 and 25.
# Servants' door = step (37, 9) (block 18,4, 28's bottom-right quadrant): side/kitchen
#   entrance for the interior's back corridor.
# Tea pavilion = step (45, 21) (cottage 14 15, optional 1-room interior or bg_event).
# Western facade: estate_western.amap, same footprint; front door moves to (25, 9).
#
# Beats: Gatekeeper at the gate; Gardener in the west beds; Maid by the servants' door;
# fountain bg_event; 3 apricorn fruit trees; maze prize + 3 maze hidden items; hidden
# item on the pavilion lawn (boardwalk or Surf). No wild grass: the estate is safe ground.
# Perimeter: a gravel walk runs inside the fence; the fence's top half is path, so that
# row reads as one strip.
# Attach: exit S (24,43) and exit W (0,38) on the outer lane. Suggested: the S exit off
# Reedmere Marsh's N exit (the marsh is the "wild" approach), or off Route 37/38.
ref EcruteakCity
key a=2c b=2a c=2d d=22 e=23 n=2b h=26 i=27 j=2f k=28 l=29
key K=ac F=82 q=48 w=49 p=4a x=14 y=15 B=89
key 1=3c 2=3d 3=3e 4=3f 5=5d 6=65 7=60 8=62 9=61 !=5c ?=5e &=64 $=66
